files via upload", "created_at": "2021-03-17T08:31:18Z", "repo": "C--programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "8ccf989baa335aaea30f81b65907b30f17fac0f0", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2021-01-11T13:18:39Z", "repo": "C--programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b6f4d3cc4f389085aad6da3206cd54ea156bdfb6", "message": "Update cellcompete.c\n\nThere is a colony of 8 cells arranged in a straight line where each day every cell\r\ncompetes with its adjacent cells (neighbour). Each day, for each cell, if its neighbours are both\r\nactive and both inactive, the cell becomes inactive the next day, otherwise it becomes active the\r\nnext day.\r\nAssumptions: The two cells on the ends have single adjacent cell, so the other adjacent cell can\r\nbe assumed to be always inactive.\r\nEven after updating the cell state. Consider its previous state for updating the state of other\r\ncells. Update the cell information of all cells simultaneously.\r\nWrite a function cell Compete which takes one 8 element array of integer\u2019s cells representing the\r\ncurrent state of 8 cells and one integer days representing the number of days to simulate.\r\nAn integer value of 1 represents an active cell and value of 0 represents an inactive cell.\r\nExisting Program\r\nint* cellCompete(int* cells,int days)\r\n{/\r\n/write your code here\r\n}\r\n//function signature ends", "created_at": "2021-01-05T17:47:59Z", "repo": "C--programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "d7f9be35ad62488b2c67f18671a48cfdc962e8ae", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2021-01-05T16:33:36Z", "repo": "C--programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "101e9c9e37b40ae47947a51398dc4feb184d53a7", "message": "Adding the File Philand file", "created_at": "2020-10-29T09:32:08Z", "repo": "C--programs", "file_sampled":